{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '325,615p'\"","aggregated_output":"   325\t(defn- shadowed?\n   326\t  [{:keys [free-env store]} sym]\n   327\t  (or (contains? free-env sym) (contains? store sym)))\n   328\t\n   329\t\n   330\t(defn- resolvable?\n   331\t  [{:keys [primitives modules]} sym]\n   332\t  (or (contains? primitives sym)\n   333\t      (and (symbol? sym)\n   334\t           (some? (namespace sym))\n   335\t           (some? (module/resolve-module\n   336\t                    modules\n   337\t                    (symbol (str (namespace sym) \".\" (name sym))))))))\n   338\t\n   339\t\n   340\t(defn free-name-defect\n   341\t  \"The first step-5 refusal for the obligation names `names` against\n   342\t   `receiver` (`{:free-env :store :primitives :modules}`, every key\n   343\t   optional), or nil when every name is bound identically by the\n   344\t   receiver.\"\n   345\t  [receiver names]\n   346\t  (some (fn [sym]\n   347\t          (cond (shadowed? receiver sym)\n   348\t                (refused :shadowed-free {:name sym})\n   349\t                (not (resolvable? receiver sym))\n   350\t                (refused :unresolved-free {:name sym})))\n   351\t        names))\n   352\t\n   353\t\n   354\t;; =============================================================================\n   355\t;; fetch (section 4)\n   356\t;; =============================================================================\n   357\t\n   358\t(def ^:private missing\n   359\t  \"Opaque per-host not-found sentinel for `jing/get`, never a keyword: a\n   360\t   keyword sentinel could collide with a genuinely stored payload.\"\n   361\t  #?(:cljd (Object.)\n   362\t     :clj (Object.)\n   363\t     :cljs (js-obj)))\n   364\t\n   365\t\n   366\t(defn- read-address\n   367\t  \"Step 2's read: the stored canonical bytes, `missing` when absent, or\n   368\t   `missing` when the handle fails (a closed client, a malformed RPC\n   369\t   envelope, a transport timeout). A failing store has no payload for this\n   370\t   caller, so it fails closed as `:absent`, never as execution. The bytes\n   371\t   are read raw through the handle's byte store, not through `jing/get`,\n   372\t   so that step 2's own address check can name the mismatch.\"\n   373\t  [handle address]\n   374\t  (try (let [get-fn (:get-bytes-fn handle)]\n   375\t         (if (fn? get-fn) (get-fn address missing) missing))\n   376\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   377\t         missing)))\n   378\t\n   379\t\n   380\t(defn- decoded\n   381\t  \"The value of canonical bytes bs, or nil when they do not decode.\"\n   382\t  [bs]\n   383\t  (try (cbor/decode bs)\n   384\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   385\t         nil)))\n   386\t\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn- byte-count\n   389\t  \"The length of host bytes bs, for the `:max-bytes` bound.\"\n   390\t  [bs]\n   391\t  #?(:clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n   392\t     :cljs (.-length bs)\n   393\t     :cljd (.-length ^typed/Uint8List bs)))\n   394\t\n   395\t\n   396\t(defn- identity-of\n   397\t  \"The identity `value` mints under the format, or nil when it cannot be\n   398\t   minted at all (a malformed payload mints no identity). Used by\n   399\t   `publish!` and for refusal evidence, never by verification: step 3 is\n   400\t   `:identity-matches-fn`, directed by the identity the request carries\n   401\t   (I5).\"\n   402\t  [format value]\n   403\t  (try ((:identity-fn format) value)\n   404\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   405\t         nil)))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t(defn- matches-identity?\n   409\t  \"Step 3's check, directed by the identity the request carries. False\n   410\t   when the payload cannot be matched at all (a malformed payload\n   411\t   matches no identity).\"\n   412\t  [format identity value]\n   413\t  (try ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity value)\n   414\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false)))\n   415\t\n   416\t\n   417\t(defn- row-defect\n   418\t  \"Step 2's per-part check, or nil when the part is locally well formed.\n   419\t   A `:row-defect-fn` that throws refuses like a validator.\"\n   420\t  [format value]\n   421\t  (try ((:row-defect-fn format) value)\n   422\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   423\t         {:rule :validator-refused})))\n   424\t\n   425\t\n   426\t(defn- validation-defect\n   427\t  [format value]\n   428\t  (try ((:validate-fn format) value)\n   429\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   430\t         {:rule :validator-refused})))\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\t(defn- fetch-one\n   434\t  \"One worklist visit: read `address` raw, verify it against the address\n   435\t   it was requested at, then validate it row-locally -- in that order, so\n   436\t   a malformed row is refused before any address it references is\n   437\t   enqueued. Returns `{:value v :bytes n}` or a refusal.\"\n   438\t  [handle format identity address]\n   439\t  (let [bs (read-address handle address)]\n   440\t    (cond\n   441\t      (identical? missing bs)\n   442\t      (refused :absent {:address address})\n   443\t\n   444\t      (not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs))\n   445\t      (refused :address-mismatch {:address address, :value (decoded bs)})\n   446\t\n   447\t      :else\n   448\t      (let [value (decoded bs)]\n   449\t        (if (nil? value)\n   450\t          (refused :address-mismatch {:address address, :value nil})\n   451\t          (if-let [defect (row-defect format value)]\n   452\t            (refused :descriptor-defect\n   453\t                     {:identity identity, :address address,\n   454\t                      :defect defect})\n   455\t            {:value value, :bytes (byte-count bs)}))))))\n   456\t\n   457\t\n   458\t(defn- fetch-parts\n   459\t  \"Step 2: the bounded breadth-first worklist from `root-address`\n   460\t   (section 4.2). `:parts-fn` names the further addresses a fetched\n   461\t   payload references; the walk enqueues them behind the current one,\n   462\t   verifies each the same way, and visits each address once. `bounds` is\n   463\t   the composition's `{:max-parts n :max-depth d :max-bytes b}`, every\n   464\t   key optional; exceeding one is `:parts-limit` naming the bound and the\n   465\t   address at which it was hit. Returns `{:parts {address body} :multi?\n   466\t   boolean}` or a refusal. `:multi?` is the record's own answer to\n   467\t   whether the format has parts at all: a single-payload format's\n   468\t   `:parts-fn` returns nil, a multi-part format's a sequence, possibly\n   469\t   empty for a leaf row.\"\n   470\t  [handle format identity root-address bounds]\n   471\t  (let [{:keys [max-parts max-depth max-bytes]} bounds]\n   472\t    (loop [queue [[root-address 0]]\n   473\t           index 0\n   474\t           parts {}\n   475\t           bytes 0\n   476\t           multi? nil]\n   477\t      (if (= index (count queue))\n   478\t        {:parts parts, :multi? (boolean multi?)}\n   479\t        (let [[address depth] (nth queue index)]\n   480\t          (if (contains? parts address)\n   481\t            (recur queue (inc index) parts bytes multi?)\n   482\t            (cond\n   483\t              (and max-parts (>= (count parts) max-parts))\n   484\t              (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-parts, :address address})\n   485\t\n   486\t              (and max-depth (> depth max-depth))\n   487\t              (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-depth, :address address})\n   488\t\n   489\t              :else\n   490\t              (let [res (fetch-one handle format identity address)]\n   491\t                (if (refused? res)\n   492\t                  res\n   493\t                  (let [value (:value res)\n   494\t                        bytes' (+ bytes (:bytes res))]\n   495\t                    (if (and max-bytes (> bytes' max-bytes))\n   496\t                      (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-bytes,\n   497\t                                             :address address})\n   498\t                      (let [child-addrs ((:parts-fn format) value)\n   499\t                            multi?' (if (nil? multi?)\n   500\t                                      (not (nil? child-addrs))\n   501\t                                      multi?)]\n   502\t                        (recur (if (seq child-addrs)\n   503\t                                 (into queue\n   504\t                                       (map (fn [a] [a (inc depth)])\n   505\t                                            (distinct child-addrs)))\n   506\t                                 queue)\n   507\t                               (inc index)\n   508\t                               (assoc parts address value)\n   509\t                               bytes'\n   510\t                               multi?')))))))))))))\n   511\t\n   512\t\n   513\t(defn fetch\n   514\t  \"Fetches and verifies an image by its identity using handle, index, and\n   515\t   format record; one surface for all four formats. Returns the verified\n   516\t   image `{:status :ok ...}` or a qualified refusal.\n   517\t\n   518\t   `handle` is any DaoJing content handle; `index` is a map or function\n   519\t   from identity to Jing address -- the identity function itself for the\n   520\t   two storage-derived formats, whose identity is its own address\n   521\t   (section 3); `format` is a format record; `identity` is H or R, a\n   522\t   root row id, or a vector address. `receiver` is the receiving VM's\n   523\t   free-name environment `{:free-env :store :primitives :modules}`; the\n   524\t   4-arity form uses the empty receiver, so only a closed image (no\n   525\t   obligations) is accepted. `opts` carries the admission contract\n   526\t   `:contract` and the step-2 bounds `:max-parts`, `:max-depth`,\n   527\t   `:max-bytes`; every key optional, a nil bound unbounded.\n   528\t\n   529\t   The steps run in strict order (section 4.2), with no format-specific\n   530\t   branching:\n   531\t     0. the requested contract equals the record's   :contract-mismatch\n   532\t     1. address <- (index identity)                  :absent\n   533\t     2. the bounded worklist of :parts-fn, each      :absent,\n   534\t        part read, verified, then row-checked        :address-mismatch,\n   535\t        before any child it names is enqueued        :descriptor-defect,\n   536\t                                                     :parts-limit\n   537\t     3. ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity root :hash-mismatch\n   538\t     4. ((:validate-fn format) whole) is nil         :descriptor-defect\n   539\t     5. every obligation binds in the receiver       :unresolved-free,\n   540\t                                                     :shadowed-free\n   541\t     6. the verified image\n   542\t\n   543\t   For a multi-part format the whole of steps 4 to 6 is the tree\n   544\t   assembled by prepending each fetched part's address, the shape\n   545\t   `validate-rows` takes (section 5.1), and the outcome carries\n   546\t   `:parts {address body}`.\"\n   547\t  ([handle index format identity]\n   548\t   (fetch handle index format identity {}))\n   549\t  ([handle index format identity receiver]\n   550\t   (fetch handle index format identity receiver nil))\n   551\t  ([handle index format identity receiver opts]\n   552\t   (let [{:keys [contract max-parts max-depth max-bytes]} opts]\n   553\t     (if (and (some? contract) (not= contract (:contract format)))\n   554\t       (refused :contract-mismatch\n   555\t                {:expected contract, :actual (:contract format)})\n   556\t       (if-let [address (index identity)]\n   557\t         (if-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n   558\t           (refused :absent {:address address})\n   559\t           (let [worklist (fetch-parts handle format identity address\n   560\t                                       {:max-parts max-parts,\n   561\t                                        :max-depth max-depth,\n   562\t                                        :max-bytes max-bytes})]\n   563\t             (if (refused? worklist)\n   564\t               worklist\n   565\t               (let [{:keys [parts multi?]} worklist\n   566\t                     root-value (get parts address)\n   567\t                     whole (if multi?\n   568\t                             {:root identity,\n   569\t                              :rows (into {}\n   570\t                                          (map (fn [[a v]] [a (into [a] v)]))\n   571\t                                          parts)}\n   572\t                             root-value)]\n   573\t                 (if-not (matches-identity? format identity root-value)\n   574\t                   (refused :hash-mismatch\n   575\t                            {:expected identity,\n   576\t                             :actual (identity-of format root-value)})\n   577\t                   (if-let [defect (validation-defect format whole)]\n   578\t                     (refused :descriptor-defect\n   579\t                              {:identity identity, :defect defect})\n   580\t                     (let [obligations ((:obligations-fn format) whole)]\n   581\t                       (or (free-name-defect receiver obligations)\n   582\t                           (merge {:status :ok,\n   583\t                                   :format (:format format),\n   584\t                                   :identity identity,\n   585\t                                   :address address,\n   586\t                                   :value whole,\n   587\t                                   :obligations obligations}\n   588\t                                  (when multi? {:parts parts}))))))))))\n   589\t         (refused :absent {:identity identity}))))))\n   590\t\n   591\t\n   592\t;; =============================================================================\n   593\t;; Publishing (the mint-side counterpart the tests and compositions use)\n   594\t;; =============================================================================\n   595\t\n   596\t(defn publish!\n   597\t  \"Store `image` in `handle` and return its index datom\n   598\t   `[identity attribute address]`. The address is the store's own\n   599\t   `segment-key`; the identity is the format's own mint. The caller owns\n   600\t   the index: nothing is recorded here. The two storage-derived formats\n   601\t   mint through `yin.vm.content` instead (section 9).\"\n   602\t  [handle format image]\n   603\t  (let [address (jing/materialize! handle image)]\n   604\t    [((:identity-fn format) image) (address-attribute format) address]))\n   605\t\n   606\t\n   607\t;; =============================================================================\n   608\t;; Same-root pairing (section 7)\n   609\t;; =============================================================================\n   610\t\n   611\t(defn pairing-datoms\n   612\t  \"The mint-time pairing datoms recorded beside a named root.\"\n   613\t  [root H R]\n   614\t  [[root :yin.debruijn.code/hash H]\n   615\t   [root :yin.debruijn.register/hash R]])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
